quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  2,283,"If you are on a journey and cannot find a scribe, then (something) may be taken into possession as security. If one of you entrusts to another, let the trustee restore the trust to its owner. He should be God-conscious, his Lord. Do not conceal testimony; whoever conceals it, his heart will indeed be sinful. And Allah is All-Knowing of what you do."
  2,284,"To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Whether you reveal whatever is in your hearts or conceal it, Allah will bring you to account for it. Then He will forgive whomever He wills and punish whomever He wills. And Allah is All-Capable of everything."
  2,285,"The Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) believes in what has been revealed to him from his Lord, and so do the believers. They all believe in Allah, His angels, His Books and His Messengers. (They declare:) ‘We make no distinction between any of His Messengers.’ And they say: ‘We hear and obey. (Grant us) Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the final return.’"
  2,286,"Allah does not burden any soul beyond its capacity. Whatever (good) it earns will be for its (own) benefit, and whatever (evil) it incurs will be its (own) loss. ‘Our Lord! Do not take us to task if we forget or make mistakes. Our Lord! Do not burden us as you burdened those before us. Our Lord! Do not burden us with more than we have the strength to bear. Excuse us, and forgive us and have mercy upon us. You are our Master. So help us against the disbelieving people.’"
